# kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=1, measured on hbox 2026-10-14) makes every sandboxed worker
# exit 1 at once, and the hermes driver then reported "Hermes ACP stream closed" after a 15-min wait: a
# missing box input rendering as a product red. The set's own deploy/grain-host/resolve-bwrap is the one
# resolver its drivers use (hermes-journey.sh, jpay6.sh, grain-journey.sh for m6grain's spk-host profile):
# the AppArmor-profiled /usr/local/libexec/mini-grain-bwrap when present and usable, else /usr/bin/bwrap;
# MINI_BWRAP selects one. The probe runs it and exports its answer, so the row and its driver resolve the
# same binary; nothing usable is 98, named. A set without the resolver pins its bwrap in its drivers:
# product_userns [LEGACY_BWRAP...] probes those (default /usr/bin/bwrap; jpay6.sh before the resolver also
# fell back to the profiled copy), and only for such a set.
product_userns() {
